 What's in this repo"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"- **`skills/upstash-*/`** — the per-SDK skill sources (each has a `SKILL.md`). Edit these.\n- **`skil"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"ls/upstash/`** — the combined skill, **generated** from all the sources by `npm run build`. Never ha"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"nd-edit it (see `AGENTS.md`).\n- **Plugin manifests** — `.claude-plugin/`, `.codex-plugin/`, `.cursor"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"-plugin/`, `gemini-extension.json`, and the portable Agent Plugins `plugin.json` + `mcp.json`. They "},{"id":"p8s5","text":"make the repo installable as a plugin/extension. **These plugins now bundle the remote Upstash MCP s"},{"id":"p8s6","text":"erver (OAuth), so installing the plugin sets up the skills *and* the MCP in one step** — no separate"},{"id":"p8s7","text":" MCP configuration for Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, or Gemini CLI.\n- **`zed-extension/`** — a Zed MCP"},{"id":"p8s8","text":" server extension (Rust → Wasm).\n- **`assets/`** — branding used on the plugin card, read by Codex ("},{"id":"p8s9","text":"`interface.logo` / `interface.composerIcon`) and Cursor (`logo`). Claude Code, Gemini CLI and the Ag"},{"id":"p8s10","text":"ent Plugins schema have no icon field."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Available Skills"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| Skill | Description |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| redis-best-practices | Performance rules for any Redis, measured on real databases: batching, big "},{"id":"p11s2","text":"keys, TTLs, scripts, connections. |\n| upstash | Combined skill covering all Upstash SDKs and CLIs. |"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"\n| upstash-blob-js | S3-compatible object storage with direct browser uploads and signed URLs. |\n| u"},{"id":"p11s4","text":"pstash-box-cli | Drive a sandboxed cloud container from the terminal with the `box` CLI. |\n| upstash"},{"id":"p11s5","text":"-box-js | Sandboxed cloud containers with AI agents, shell, filesystem, and git. |\n| upstash-box-py "},{"id":"p11s6","text":"| The same sandboxed cloud containers, from the Python SDK. |\n| upstash-box-remote-work | Do work in"},{"id":"p11s7","text":" a sandboxed cloud Box over the remote MCP, with preview URLs, screenshots, and PRs. |\n| upstash-cli"},{"id":"p11s8","text":" | Drive the Upstash Developer API from the terminal with the `upstash` CLI. |\n| upstash-qstash-js |"},{"id":"p11s9","text":" Serverless messaging and scheduling via HTTP endpoints. |\n| upstash-ratelimit-js | Rate limiting wi"},{"id":"p11s10","text":"th the Redis Rate Limit TypeScript SDK. |\n| upstash-redis-js | Serverless Redis — caching, sessions,"},{"id":"p11s11","text":" leaderboards, full-text search. |\n| upstash-redis-start | Provision a zero-config, no-signup scratc"},{"id":"p11s12","text":"h Redis database for an agent. |\n| upstash-search-js | Full-text search quick starts, core concepts,"},{"id":"p11s13","text":" and TypeScript SDK. |\n| upstash-vector-js | Vector database features, SDK usage, and framework inte"},{"id":"p11s14","text":"grations. |\n| upstash-workflow-js | Durable workflows — define, trigger, and manage multi-step proce"},{"id":"p11s15","text":"s. |\n| upstash-workflow-js | Durable workflows — define, trigger, and manage multi-step processes. |"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Installing through a **plugin** (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Gemini CLI) sets up both the skills and"},{"id":"p13s2","text":" the remote MCP server — approve the MCP's OAuth consent on first use. The skills-only installers (A"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"gent Skills CLI, OpenCode, Zed) install skills; add the MCP server separately if you want live accou"},{"id":"p13s4","text":"nt access, or use `npx upstash`, which sets up both."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"For the full, up-to-date per-client instructions, see Install by agent."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"### One command (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Gemini CLI, VS Code, Copilot CLI, OpenCode)"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Run in a terminal, the Upstash CLI detects your agents and installs the plugin where the agent suppo"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"rts one (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Gemini CLI), otherwise the remote MCP server plus the `upstash`"},{"id":"p17s3","text":" skill (VS Code, Copilot CLI, OpenCode). Either way the agent gets both the skills and the MCP serve"},{"id":"p17s4","text":"r, which signs in with OAuth on first use. The per-agent steps below do the same by hand."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"From an agent or a script, name the agent and skip the prompts:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"### Claude Code (skills + MCP)"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"### OpenAI Codex (skills + MCP)"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"### Cursor (skills + MCP)"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"We are waiting for this plugin to be accepted to the official\nCursor Marketplace. Once listed, it ca"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"n be installed\nfrom **Customize** in the Cursor sidebar, and it brings both the skills and the MCP s"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"erver.\nUntil then, `npx upstash setup --cursor` installs the same plugin locally (reload the Cursor "},{"id":"p25s4","text":"`npx upstash setup --cursor` installs the same plugin locally (reload the Cursor window afterwards)."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"### Gemini CLI (skills + MCP)"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"Gemini CLI loads this repo as an extension — the manifest is `gemini-extension.json` at the repo roo"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"t; every skill under `skills/` and the remote MCP server are picked up automatically:"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"### OpenCode"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"OpenCode loads Agent Skills from `.agents/skills/` in a project\nand `~/.config/opencode/skills/` glo"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"bally, which is where the Agent Skills CLI writes them for\nOpenCode:"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"OpenCode exposes the installed skills to the agent through its native `skill` tool, so the\nagent loa"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"ds only the sub-skill relevant to the task at hand. For live access to your account\n(create database"},{"id":"p32s3","text":"s, inspect QStash logs, and so on), add the MCP server as well, or run\n`npx upstash setup --opencode"},{"id":"p32s4","text":"`, which installs the skill and adds the MCP server in one step."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"### Zed"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"Zed loads Agent Skills from `.agents/skills/` in a project\nand `~/.agents/skills/` globally, which i"},{"id":"p34s2","text":"s exactly where the Agent Skills CLI writes them:"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"The skills then show up in Zed's Agent Panel, and the agent can load them on its own or via\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}

